WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.200
The Revolutionary Armed Forces of

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.920
Colombia, the FARC, is the guerrilla organization

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.640
that the administration of Juan Manuel Santos has

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.640
negotiated a peace agreement with.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.100
The FARC dates back 52 years, founded to

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:20.939
wage an insurrection against the

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:23.249
democratic institutions of Colombia,

00:00:23.249 --> 00:00:25.169
attacking the oligarchic political

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:28.869
system and economic system through the use of force.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.100
In the mid-1990s,

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.220
the FARC evolved into the

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.300
biggest cocaine smuggling organization in the world,

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.500
and they used this to generate revenue.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.380
The FARC is not a

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.380
popular organization by any means today.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.400
They probably command less than

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.870
three or four percent of the vote.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.260
The question is, with the opportunity to

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.060
establish a presence on the ground

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.680
unassailed by the government,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.420
will they build up their base of popular support?

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.810
Undermine confidence in the democratic

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.250
institutions in the elected government

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.130
of Colombia,  which is south America's

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.660
oldest democracy.

